# Intentionally minimal.
#
# This file used to carry `legacy-peer-deps=true`, added in Phase 0 to work
# around react-konva@18.2.10 declaring a peer range of konva ^7/^8/^9 while this
# project runs konva ^10. That was never a fix — it told npm to ignore a real
# conflict.
#
# Resolved properly in Phase 4.5: react-konva 19.0.8 was the first release whose
# peer range includes konva ^10.0.0, and 19.0.x still accepts React ^18.3.1, so
# no React upgrade is needed. The dependency is pinned to ~19.0.10 rather than
# ^19.0.10 on purpose — react-konva 19.2.x raises its React peer to ^19.2.0, and
# a caret range would drift onto it. There is no 19.1.x.
